<title>HUNGARY: OTP Q1 AFTER-TAX PROFIT UP AT HUF 4.93BLN.</title>
<headline>OTP Q1 AFTER-TAX PROFIT UP AT HUF 4.93BLN.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three-month period ending</p>
<p>on March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>						Q1 1997	 Q1 1996</p>
<p>    Group operating profit	     6,059   vs   4,222</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		 6,040   vs   4,059</p>
<p>    Group after-tax profit	     4,928   vs   3,191</p>
<p>    Group general reserves created     428   vs     887</p>
<p>    Group dividend paid		    807   vs     840</p>
<p>    Group net profit		     3,693   vs   1,464</p>
<p>    Group interest received	   53,820   vs  50,330</p>
<p>    Group interest paid		 38,912   vs  35,688</p>
<p>    Group interest margin	     14,908   vs  14,643</p>
<p>Group profit from financial</p>
<p>	and investment services	  7,191   vs   4,950</p>
<p>Group loss from non-financial</p>
<p>	non-investment services	  1,132 loss vs  728 loss</p>
<p>    Group extraordinary loss		19 loss vs  163 loss</p>
<p>NOTE: The figures are non-audited, concolidated and were</p>
<p>calculated according to the Hungarian accounting standard. Full</p>
<p>company name is Orszagos Takarekpenztar es Kereskedelmi Bank</p>
<p>Rt.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
